# .ctsignore — gitignore-syntax paths that `cts-sync.sh update` will never touch.
# Use for: customized CTS files, pruned CTS files (prevents re-adding them),
# and project-only additions placed under payload directories.
#
# Two-layer model (migrated 2026-07-23): former whole-file customizations
# (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, rules/{code-style,migrations-queue,testing,
# validation-authorization,workflow}.md, .claude/agents/{reviewer,tester,
# queue-specialist}.md, .claude/settings.json) now live as override files
# instead — AGENTS.local.md, CLAUDE.local.md, rules/local/*.md,
# .claude/agents-local/*.md. Those upstream paths are no longer ignored here
# and receive plain CTS overwrites, with the overrides layered on top per the
# lex-specialis convention. .claude/settings.json is jq deep-merged from
# .cts/settings.cts.json by the sync engine itself — never ignored.

# pruned — HPW has no frontend/UI; re-add from CTS if a UI ever appears
.claude/agents/vue-developer.md
.claude/agents/react-developer.md
.claude/agents/angular-developer.md
.claude/skills/vue-expert/
.claude/skills/react-expert/
.claude/skills/angular-expert/

# customized — HPW is pure Jest (jest.config.ts/.cts in every app/lib,
# jest/ts-jest/@swc/jest deps, zero vitest in package.json), so this is a
# whole-file fork of the shipped skill.
#
# NOTE (claude-ts 0.2.0): the reason this fork existed — "no lex-specialis
# override mechanism exists for skills" — no longer holds. CTS now ships
# .claude/skills-local/<name>/SKILL.md as the skills override layer, and
# vitest-testing was its pilot. Retiring this fork in favour of
# .claude/skills-local/vitest-testing/SKILL.md (vi.fn → jest.fn, nx test in
# place of npx vitest run) removes the whole-file fork and stops the recurring
# "ignored, but changed upstream" report on every sync. Not yet done.
.claude/skills/vitest-testing/

# customized — project-specific additions with no lex-specialis override
# mechanism (plain payload file, not rules/** or .claude/agents/**). The
# 2026-07-23 first sync under the new engine overwrote this before the
# .ctsignore entry existed (no prior manifest baseline to detect drift
# against) — content was manually restored from git history afterward.
/.prettierignore

# customized — HPW's own /fix-ci and /review-pr predate CTS claiming
# .claude/commands/ as payload (claude-ts 3ea81a0). Both carry real local
# adaptations CTS's copies lack: fix-ci.md is Nx-aware (nx typecheck/lint per
# project, ~63 differing lines), and both point reviewers at the two-layer
# override files (CLAUDE.local.md, rules/local/**) that upstream's copies
# still omit. Protect them until those improvements are contributed upstream,
# then drop these two entries and take CTS's copies.
/.claude/commands/fix-ci.md
/.claude/commands/review-pr.md
